    "Description": "Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6 is a standalone server, based on the Keycloak\nproject, that provides authentication and standards-based single sign-on\ncapabilities for web and mobile applications.\n\nThis release of Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6.14 on RHEL 9 serves as a replacement\nfor Red Hat Single Sign-On 7.6.13, and includes bug fixes and enhancements,\nwhich are documented in the Release Notes document linked to in the References.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n* Unauthenticated account takeover via reset-credentials flow bypass (CVE-2026-18963)",
